1. **An additive manufacturing method**, comprising:

   forming, by additive manufacturing, a green metal article comprising a metal part having a hole extending through or into the metal part;

   during the forming of the green metal article, forming a removable internal support within the hole;

   forming a first ceramic release layer between a lower surface of the removable internal support and an adjacent surface of the metal part;

   forming a second ceramic release layer between an upper surface of the removable internal support and another adjacent surface of the metal part;

   sintering the green metal article with the removable internal support positioned within the hole, wherein the removable internal support supports the metal part during sintering to inhibit distortion of the hole or surrounding metal part; and

   after sintering, removing the removable internal support from the hole,

   wherein the first and second ceramic release layers inhibit bonding between the removable internal support and the metal part during sintering to facilitate removal of the removable internal support.

1. A method comprising:  

3D printing, using a metal-containing build material, a green part defining a hole extending at least partially through the green part;  

during the 3D printing, depositing a model-material support within the hole such that the model-material support supports at least a portion of the green part surrounding the hole;  

forming one or more release-material layers between the model-material support and the portion of the green part surrounding the hole, the one or more release-material layers comprising ceramic powder and a binder; and  

sintering an assembly comprising the green part, the model-material support, and the one or more release-material layers to produce a sintered metal part surrounding the hole, wherein the one or more release-material layers inhibit bonding between the sintered metal part and the model-material support.

What is claimed is:

1. A method of reducing distortion of a hole in a three-dimensionally printed metal part during sintering, the method comprising:  
   forming, by additive manufacturing, a green part comprising a metal model material and defining a hole;  
   concurrently forming, by the additive manufacturing, a support structure positioned at least partially within the hole, the support structure comprising the same metal model material as the green part;  
   depositing one or more ceramic release layers between the support structure and an inner wall of the hole, the one or more ceramic release layers being configured to inhibit metallurgical bonding between the support structure and the inner wall during sintering;  
   sintering the green part and the support structure together, wherein the support structure mechanically supports the inner wall of the hole during the sintering to limit deformation of the hole; and  
   after sintering, removing the support structure from the hole, the one or more ceramic release layers facilitating separation of the support structure from the sintered metal part.
